{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_vfICbse7JXLpG4g0nkPamgfs","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# session-protocol Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→Define the session lifecycle protocol for SE 3.0 agents. This spec governs progressive startup (se3 status → progress.md → scope determination), execution boundaries, shutdown procedures, and tool-enforced progress tracking across sessions.\n     5→## Requirements\n     6→### Requirement: Session Startup Protocol\n     7→The system SHALL define a progressive session startup protocol. The agent MUST locate current state with minimal context, then load more on demand.\n     8→\n     9→Startup steps:\n    10→1. Verify `openspec` CLI is available; if not, ask the human to install it. If available but `openspec/` directory does not exist, run `openspec init`.\n    11→2. Run `se3 status` for computed project state (git, collab, human-calls)\n    12→3. Read `head -50 progress.md` + `git log --oneline -5`\n    13→4. Scan `human-calls/` for responded but unprocessed requests\n    14→5. Check `openspec/changes/` for active changes and `openspec/specs/` for current capabilities\n    15→6. Determine session scope based on progress \"next steps\" + active changes\n    16→7. Load additional files only when the task requires them\n    17→\n    18→If step 3 finds no progress.md and no git history → **first-time bootstrap**:\n    19→- Ask the human (sync human call): \"What should this project do?\"\n    20→- Create an openspec change from the response (proposal captures the intent)\n    21→- Create `progress.md`\n    22→\n    23→#### Scenario: OpenSpec not installed\n    24→- **WHEN** agent starts a session and `openspec` command is not found\n    25→- **THEN** agent asks the human to install it via sync human call and does not proceed with spec-related work until resolved\n    26→\n    27→#### Scenario: OpenSpec not initialized\n    28→- **WHEN** agent starts a session and `openspec` is available but `openspec/` directory does not exist\n    29→- **THEN** agent runs `openspec init` before proceeding\n    30→\n    31→#### Scenario: Mature project startup\n    32→- **WHEN** agent starts a session with existing progress.md and git history\n    33→- **THEN** agent runs `se3 status`, reads progress.md and git log, then determines scope without reading all spec files upfront\n    34→\n    35→#### Scenario: First-time bootstrap\n    36→- **WHEN** agent starts a session with no progress.md and no git history\n    37→- **THEN** agent asks the human what to build via human call, creates an openspec change from the response\n    38→\n    39→#### Scenario: On-demand deep loading\n    40→- **WHEN** agent needs details about a specific capability during execution\n    41→- **THEN** agent reads the relevant spec file at that point, not during startup\n    42→\n    43→### Requirement: Session Execution Boundary\n    44→Each session MUST focus on a limited scope of work and MUST NOT attempt to complete too many tasks in a single session.\n    45→\n    46→#### Scenario: Session scope limitation\n    47→- **WHEN** the agent has determined the work scope through the startup protocol\n    48→- **THEN** the agent only executes tasks within that scope and does not actively expand the scope\n    49→\n    50→### Requirement: Session Shutdown Protocol\n    51→Session ending MUST leave code in a mergeable state. Progress tracking is handled automatically by tools.\n    52→\n    53→Shutdown steps:\n    54→1. Ensure all modified code runs correctly\n    55→2. Run `se3 handoff` — automatically commits and generates session summary in progress.md\n    56→3. Update openspec change status if applicable\n    57→\n    58→### Requirement: Session Commit Cadence\n    59→\n    60→The system SHALL define when commits occur during a session.\n    61→\n    62→Commits SHOULD occur mid-session when a distinct, working unit of change is complete — not accumulated into a single commit with unrelated changes.\n    63→\n    64→**When to commit mid-session:**\n    65→- After completing a coherent unit of work that passes tests\n    66→- Before starting a substantially different task that would muddy the commit message\n    67→- Before context clearing (/new) if there are completed changes to preserve\n    68→\n    69→**Commit sequence:**\n    70→1. Run tests — do NOT commit with failing tests\n    71→2. Stage files\n    72→3. Write message with context for next session\n    73→4. Commit (via `se3 commit` — automatically appends progress entry)\n    74→\n    75→**Commit Rules:**\n    76→- Commit when a meaningful unit of work is complete — not tied to /new or any mechanical trigger\n    77→- Do not batch unrelated changes into one commit\n    78→- Commit messages MUST include summary of changes and context for the next session\n    79→\n    80→#### Scenario: Mid-session commit\n    81→- **WHEN** a distinct unit of work is complete and tested\n    82→- **THEN** agent commits before starting the next unit\n    83→\n    84→### Requirement: Session Context Clearing\n    85→\n    86→The system SHALL define when context is cleared during a session.\n    87→\n    88→Context SHOULD be cleared when it approaches saturation or when switching to a substantially different task.\n    89→\n    90→Context SHOULD NOT be cleared mechanically after every task group — agents SHOULD continue if there is context budget and the next task benefits from current context.\n    91→\n    92→#### Scenario: Normal shutdown\n    93→- **WHEN** agent completes the current scope\n    94→- **THEN** agent runs `se3 handoff`, code is mergeable, progress is updated automatically\n    95→\n    96→#### Scenario: Context approaching saturation\n    97→- **WHEN** context window is nearly full\n    98→- **THEN** agent prioritizes shutdown protocol (at minimum: `se3 commit` current work)\n    99→\n   100→### Requirement: Progress Tracking File\n   101→The system SHALL use progress.md as the cumulative cross-session progress record. Progress entries are appended automatically by `se3 commit` and `se3 handoff` — agents do NOT manually maintain progress.md.\n   102→\n   103→progress.md contains:\n   104→- Auto-appended commit entries in \"Current Session\" section (by `se3 commit`)\n   105→- Formal session records generated by `se3 handoff`\n   106→- Collab session reports generated by orchestrator do_complete()\n   107→\n   108→#### Scenario: Auto-append commit entry\n   109→- **WHEN** `se3 commit` succeeds\n   110→- **THEN** a one-line commit record is automatically appended to progress.md Current Session section\n   111→\n   112→#### Scenario: Finalize session\n   113→- **WHEN** `se3 handoff` is executed\n   114→- **THEN** the Current Session section is replaced with a formal dated session record including commits, files changed, and next steps\n   115→\n   116→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7897612-31ab-4f4a-a03f-342cdc1f8a45","uuid":"44379945-57fe-4b5a-9f33-45dffdbf512d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/openspec-cli-commands/openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md","content":"# session-protocol Specification\n\n## Purpose\nDefine the session lifecycle protocol for SE 3.0 agents. This spec governs progressive startup (se3 status → progress.md → scope determination), execution boundaries, shutdown procedures, and tool-enforced progress tracking across sessions.\n## Requirements\n### Requirement: Session Startup Protocol\nThe system SHALL define a progressive session startup protocol. The agent MUST locate current state with minimal context, then load more on demand.\n\nStartup steps:\n1. Verify `openspec` CLI is available; if not, ask the human to install it. If available but `openspec/` directory does not exist, run `openspec init`.\n2. Run `se3 status` for computed project state (git, collab, human-calls)\n3. Read `head -50 progress.md` + `git log --oneline -5`\n4. Scan `human-calls/` for responded but unprocessed requests\n5. Check `openspec/changes/` for active changes and `openspec/specs/` for current capabilities\n6. Determine session scope based on progress \"next steps\" + active changes\n7. Load additional files only when the task requires them\n\nIf step 3 finds no progress.md and no git history → **first-time bootstrap**:\n- Ask the human (sync human call): \"What should this project do?\"\n- Create an openspec change from the response (proposal captures the intent)\n- Create `progress.md`\n\n#### Scenario: OpenSpec not installed\n- **WHEN** agent starts a session and `openspec` command is not found\n- **THEN** agent asks the human to install it via sync human call and does not proceed with spec-related work until resolved\n\n#### Scenario: OpenSpec not initialized\n- **WHEN** agent starts a session and `openspec` is available but `openspec/` directory does not exist\n- **THEN** agent runs `openspec init` before proceeding\n\n#### Scenario: Mature project startup\n- **WHEN** agent starts a session with existing progress.md and git history\n- **THEN** agent runs `se3 status`, reads progress.md and git log, then determines scope without reading all spec files upfront\n\n#### Scenario: First-time bootstrap\n- **WHEN** agent starts a session with no progress.md and no git history\n- **THEN** agent asks the human what to build via human call, creates an openspec change from the response\n\n#### Scenario: On-demand deep loading\n- **WHEN** agent needs details about a specific capability during execution\n- **THEN** agent reads the relevant spec file at that point, not during startup\n\n### Requirement: Session Execution Boundary\nEach session MUST focus on a limited scope of work and MUST NOT attempt to complete too many tasks in a single session.\n\n#### Scenario: Session scope limitation\n- **WHEN** the agent has determined the work scope through the startup protocol\n- **THEN** the agent only executes tasks within that scope and does not actively expand the scope\n\n### Requirement: Session Shutdown Protocol\nSession ending MUST leave code in a mergeable state. Progress tracking is handled automatically by tools.\n\nShutdown steps:\n1. Ensure all modified code runs correctly\n2. Run `se3 handoff` — automatically commits and generates session summary in progress.md\n3. Update openspec change status if applicable\n\n### Requirement: Session Commit Cadence\n\nThe system SHALL define when commits occur during a session.\n\nCommits SHOULD occur mid-session when a distinct, working unit of change is complete — not accumulated into a single commit with unrelated changes.\n\n**When to commit mid-session:**\n- After completing a coherent unit of work that passes tests\n- Before starting a substantially different task that would muddy the commit message\n- Before context clearing (/new) if there are completed changes to preserve\n\n**Commit sequence:**\n1. Run tests — do NOT commit with failing tests\n2. Stage files\n3. Write message with context for next session\n4. Commit (via `se3 commit` — automatically appends progress entry)\n\n**Commit Rules:**\n- Commit when a meaningful unit of work is complete — not tied to /new or any mechanical trigger\n- Do not batch unrelated changes into one commit\n- Commit messages MUST include summary of changes and context for the next session\n\n#### Scenario: Mid-session commit\n- **WHEN** a distinct unit of work is complete and tested\n- **THEN** agent commits before starting the next unit\n\n### Requirement: Session Context Clearing\n\nThe system SHALL define when context is cleared during a session.\n\nContext SHOULD be cleared when it approaches saturation or when switching to a substantially different task.\n\nContext SHOULD NOT be cleared mechanically after every task group — agents SHOULD continue if there is context budget and the next task benefits from current context.\n\n#### Scenario: Normal shutdown\n- **WHEN** agent completes the current scope\n- **THEN** agent runs `se3 handoff`, code is mergeable, progress is updated automatically\n\n#### Scenario: Context approaching saturation\n- **WHEN** context window is nearly full\n- **THEN** agent prioritizes shutdown protocol (at minimum: `se3 commit` current work)\n\n### Requirement: Progress Tracking File\nThe system SHALL use progress.md as the cumulative cross-session progress record. Progress entries are appended automatically by `se3 commit` and `se3 handoff` — agents do NOT manually maintain progress.md.\n\nprogress.md contains:\n- Auto-appended commit entries in \"Current Session\" section (by `se3 commit`)\n- Formal session records generated by `se3 handoff`\n- Collab session reports generated by orchestrator do_complete()\n\n#### Scenario: Auto-append commit entry\n- **WHEN** `se3 commit` succeeds\n- **THEN** a one-line commit record is automatically appended to progress.md Current Session section\n\n#### Scenario: Finalize session\n- **WHEN** `se3 handoff` is executed\n- **THEN** the Current Session section is replaced with a formal dated session record including commits, files changed, and next steps\n\n","numLines":116,"startLine":1,"totalLines":116}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_lqblYYxV06i0QobS1iXniFVV","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"SE 3.0 CLI - Main entry point for se3 commands.\"\"\"\n     2→\n     3→import json\n     4→from pathlib import Path\n     5→from typing import Optional\n     6→\n     7→import typer\n     8→\n     9→from . import __version__, SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION\n    10→\n    11→def get_framework_version() -> str:\n    12→    \"\"\"Get current framework version from single source of truth (direct file read for git worktree compatibility).\"\"\"\n    13→    import os\n    14→    from pathlib import Path\n    15→    import re\n    16→\n    17→    # Get the path to __init__.py in the current working tree\n    18→    init_file = Path(__file__).parent / \"__init__.py\"\n    19→    if not init_file.exists():\n    20→        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Cannot find se3_tools __init__.py at {init_file}\")\n    21→\n    22→    with open(init_file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    23→        content = f.read()\n    24→\n    25→    match = re.search(r'SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION\\s*=\\s*\"([\\d]+\\.[\\d]+\\.[\\d]+)\"', content)\n    26→    if not match:\n    27→        raise ValueError(\"Cannot find SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION definition in __init__.py\")\n    28→\n    29→    return match.group(1)\n    30→from .commands import lint, status, sync, verify, update, collab, commit, openspec, human_calls_cmd, human_input\n    31→from .commands.update import get_installed_se3_version\n    32→from .commands.init import initialize_project\n    33→\n    34→app = typer.Typer(\n    35→    name=\"se3\",\n    36→    help=\"SE 3.0 framework CLI tools\",\n    37→    invoke_without_command=True,\n    38→)\n    39→\n    40→def _version_callback(value: bool):\n    41→    \"\"\"Handle --version flag.\"\"\"\n    42→    if value:\n    43→        typer.echo(f\"se3 CLI version: {__version__}\")\n    44→        typer.echo(f\"SE3 Framework version: {get_framework_version()}\")\n    45→        try:\n    46→            installed = get_installed_se3_version()\n    47→            if installed != \"0.0.0\":\n    48→                typer.echo(f\"Project SE3 version: {installed}\")\n    49→        except Exception:\n    50→            pass\n    51→        raise typer.Exit()\n    52→\n    53→@app.callback()\n    54→def main(\n    55→    ctx: typer.Context,\n    56→    version: bool = typer.Option(\n    57→        False, \"--version\", \"-v\", help=\"Show version information\", callback=_version_callback, is_eager=True\n    58→    ),\n    59→):\n    60→    \"\"\"SE 3.0 framework CLI tools.\"\"\"\n    61→    if ctx.invoked_subcommand is None:\n    62→        typer.echo(ctx.get_help())\n    63→        raise typer.Exit()\n    64→\n    65→\n    66→# Register direct commands\n    67→@app.command(name=\"init\")\n    68→def init_cmd(\n    69→    force: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--force\", \"-f\", help=\"Reinitialize even if already initialized\"),\n    70→    offline: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--offline\", \"-o\", help=\"Use local templates without network\"),\n    71→    with_config: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--with-config\", \"-c\", help=\"Create se3.config.yaml\"),\n    72→    se3_version: str = typer.Option(SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION, \"--se3-version\", \"-v\", help=\"Specify SE3 version to use\"),\n    73→):\n    74→    \"\"\"Initialize a new SE 3.0 project.\"\"\"\n    75→    try:\n    76→        initialize_project(force, offline, with_config, se3_version)\n    77→    except Exception as e:\n    78→        typer.echo(\n    79→            typer.style(\n    80→                f\"Error during initialization: {str(e)}\",\n    81→                fg=typer.colors.RED,\n    82→            )\n    83→        )\n    84→        raise typer.Exit(1)\n    85→\n    86→# Register sub-typer commands (complex multi-command tools)\n    87→app.add_typer(lint.app, name=\"lint\", help=\"Lint OpenSpec files\")\n    88→app.add_typer(status.app, name=\"status\", help=\"Check project status\")\n    89→app.add_typer(sync.app, name=\"sync\", help=\"Sync output files\")\n    90→app.add_typer(verify.app, name=\"verify\", help=\"Verify spec coverage\")\n    91→app.add_typer(update.app, name=\"update\", help=\"Update SE 3.0 framework to latest version\")\n    92→app.add_typer(collab.app, name=\"collab\", help=\"Manage git-worktree multi-agent collaboration\")\n    93→app.add_typer(commit.app, name=\"commit\", help=\"Commit changes with SE3 verification\")\n    94→app.add_typer(openspec.app, name=\"openspec\", help=\"Manage OpenSpec directory and specs\")\n    95→app.add_typer(human_calls_cmd.app, name=\"human-calls\", help=\"Manage human calls\")\n    96→app.add_typer(human_input.app, name=\"human\", help=\"Manage human input\")\n    97→\n    98→# Register direct commands (simple single-command tools with positional args)\n    99→# These are registered as direct commands to avoid sub-typer nesting issues\n   100→@app.command(name=\"start\")\n   101→def start_cmd(\n   102→    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n   103→    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n   104→):\n   105→    \"\"\"Start an SE3 session — compute state and return actions for the agent.\"\"\"\n   106→    from .commands.start import run_session_start, print_text_report, print_json_report\n   107→    import json\n   108→    state = run_session_start(project_root)\n   109→    if format == \"json\":\n   110→        print_json_report(state)\n   111→    else:\n   112→        print_text_report(state)\n   113→    raise typer.Exit(code=0 if not state.get(\"actions\") else 1)\n   114→\n   115→@app.command(name=\"work\")\n   116→def work_cmd(\n   117→    change_name: Optional[str] = typer.Argument(None, help=\"Name of the change to work on\"),\n   118→    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n   119→    new: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--new\", help=\"Create new change with workflow type (bugfix/feature/review/directive)\"),\n   120→    advance: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--advance\", \"-a\", help=\"Mark current step complete and advance to next\"),\n   121→    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n   122→):\n   123→    \"\"\"Start or continue working on a change — the SDD workflow driver.\"\"\"\n   124→    from .commands.work import run_work, print_text_report, print_json_report\n   125→    result = run_work(project_root, change_name, new, advance)\n   126→    if format == \"json\":\n   127→        print_json_report(result)\n   128→    else:\n   129→        print_text_report(result)\n   130→    raise typer.Exit(code=0 if result.get(\"change\") else 1)\n   131→\n   132→@app.command(name=\"done\")\n   133→def done_cmd(\n   134→    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n   135→    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n   136→):\n   137→    \"\"\"End an SE3 session — compute shutdown actions for the agent.\"\"\"\n   138→    from .commands.done import run_session_done, print_text_report, print_json_report\n   139→    state = run_session_done(project_root)\n   140→    if format == \"json\":\n   141→        print_json_report(state)\n   142→    else:\n   143→        print_text_report(state)\n   144→    raise typer.Exit(code=0)\n   145→\n   146→def _full_cycle_cmd_impl(\n   147→    description: str,\n   148→    project_root: str,\n   149→    quick: bool,\n   150→    format: str,\n   151→):\n   152→    \"\"\"Implementation of full-cycle command.\"\"\"\n   153→    from .commands.fullcycle import run_full_cycle, print_text_report as fullcycle_print_text, print_json_report as fullcycle_print_json\n   154→    result = run_full_cycle(description, project_root, quick)\n   155→    if format == \"json\":\n   156→        fullcycle_print_json(result)\n   157→    else:\n   158→        fullcycle_print_text(result)\n   159→    raise typer.Exit(code=0 if result.get(\"success\") else 1)\n   160→\n   161→\n   162→@app.command(name=\"full-cycle\")\n   163→def full_cycle_cmd(\n   164→    description: str = typer.Argument(..., help=\"Description of the work to do\"),\n   165→    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n   166→    quick: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--quick\", \"-q\", help=\"Quick mode - skip formal change creation, use 'small' workflow\"),\n   167→    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n   168→):\n   169→    \"\"\"Run the complete start-work-done workflow in one command.\n   170→\n   171→    This command streamlines simple/quick tasks by combining:\n   172→    1. se3 start - Initialize the session\n   173→    2. se3 work --new - Create a change for the work\n   174→    3. Implementation (performed by agent)\n   175→    4. se3 done - Complete the session\n   176→\n   177→    Examples:\n   178→        se3 full-cycle \"fix login bug\"\n   179→        se3 full-cycle \"add user profile page\" --quick\n   180→        se3 full-cycle \"update documentation\" -q --json\n   181→    \"\"\"\n   182→    _full_cycle_cmd_impl(description, project_root, quick, format)\n   183→\n   184→\n   185→@app.command(name=\"fc\")\n   186→def fc_cmd(\n   187→    description: str = typer.Argument(..., help=\"Description of the work to do\"),\n   188→    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n   189→    quick: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--quick\", \"-q\", help=\"Quick mode - skip formal change creation, use 'small' workflow\"),\n   190→    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n   191→):\n   192→    \"\"\"Alias for 'full-cycle' - Run the complete start-work-done workflow in one command.\"\"\"\n   193→    _full_cycle_cmd_impl(description, project_root, quick, format)\n   194→\n   195→# Register handoff as a direct command (not a sub-typer)\n   196→@app.command(name=\"handoff\")\n   197→def handoff_cmd(\n   198→    message: Optional[str] = typer.Argument(None, help=\"Handoff message describing what was done\"),\n   199→    project_root: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Project root directory\"),\n   200→    dry_run: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--dry-run\", help=\"Preview what would happen without executing\"),\n   201→    skip_commit: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--skip-commit\", help=\"Skip automatic commit (use with caution)\"),\n   202→):\n   203→    \"\"\"Handoff control to human — enforcing SE3 commit-before-handoff rule.\"\"\"\n   204→    from .commands.handoff import handoff\n   205→    handoff(message=message, project_root=project_root, dry_run=dry_run, skip_commit=skip_commit)\n   206→\n   207→\n   208→@app.command(name=\"claude-cmd\")\n   209→def claude_cmd(\n   210→    all_cmds: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--all\", help=\"Output all commands as JSON sorted by priority\"),\n   211→    next_after: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--next\", help=\"Output the next command after the given one\"),\n   212→    project_root: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Project root directory\"),\n   213→):\n   214→    \"\"\"Show configured Claude commands by priority.\n   215→\n   216→    Used by bash scripts to resolve which Claude command to use.\n   217→    \"\"\"\n   218→    from .config import load_claude_commands\n   219→\n   220→    root = Path(project_root) if project_root else Path.cwd()\n   221→    commands = load_claude_commands(root)\n   222→\n   223→    if all_cmds:\n   224→        typer.echo(json.dumps(commands))\n   225→    elif next_after:\n   226→        found = False\n   227→        for i, entry in enumerate(commands):\n   228→            if entry[\"cmd\"] == next_after:\n   229→                if i + 1 < len(commands):\n   230→                    typer.echo(commands[i + 1][\"cmd\"])\n   231→                else:\n   232→                    typer.echo(\"\")  # No next command\n   233→                found = True\n   234→                break\n   235→        if not found:\n   236→            typer.echo(\"\")  # Command not in list\n   237→    else:\n   238→        # Default: output highest-priority command\n   239→        typer.echo(commands[0][\"cmd\"])\n   240→\n   241→\n   242→if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n   243→    app()\n   244→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7897612-31ab-4f4a-a03f-342cdc1f8a45","uuid":"048d6011-ad1a-4757-9236-8f5a9c01a103","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/openspec-cli-commands/tools/se3_tools/cli.py","content":"\"\"\"SE 3.0 CLI - Main entry point for se3 commands.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nimport typer\n\nfrom . import __version__, SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION\n\ndef get_framework_version() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Get current framework version from single source of truth (direct file read for git worktree compatibility).\"\"\"\n    import os\n    from pathlib import Path\n    import re\n\n    # Get the path to __init__.py in the current working tree\n    init_file = Path(__file__).parent / \"__init__.py\"\n    if not init_file.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Cannot find se3_tools __init__.py at {init_file}\")\n\n    with open(init_file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        content = f.read()\n\n    match = re.search(r'SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION\\s*=\\s*\"([\\d]+\\.[\\d]+\\.[\\d]+)\"', content)\n    if not match:\n        raise ValueError(\"Cannot find SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION definition in __init__.py\")\n\n    return match.group(1)\nfrom .commands import lint, status, sync, verify, update, collab, commit, openspec, human_calls_cmd, human_input\nfrom .commands.update import get_installed_se3_version\nfrom .commands.init import initialize_project\n\napp = typer.Typer(\n    name=\"se3\",\n    help=\"SE 3.0 framework CLI tools\",\n    invoke_without_command=True,\n)\n\ndef _version_callback(value: bool):\n    \"\"\"Handle --version flag.\"\"\"\n    if value:\n        typer.echo(f\"se3 CLI version: {__version__}\")\n        typer.echo(f\"SE3 Framework version: {get_framework_version()}\")\n        try:\n            installed = get_installed_se3_version()\n            if installed != \"0.0.0\":\n                typer.echo(f\"Project SE3 version: {installed}\")\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        raise typer.Exit()\n\n@app.callback()\ndef main(\n    ctx: typer.Context,\n    version: bool = typer.Option(\n        False, \"--version\", \"-v\", help=\"Show version information\", callback=_version_callback, is_eager=True\n    ),\n):\n    \"\"\"SE 3.0 framework CLI tools.\"\"\"\n    if ctx.invoked_subcommand is None:\n        typer.echo(ctx.get_help())\n        raise typer.Exit()\n\n\n# Register direct commands\n@app.command(name=\"init\")\ndef init_cmd(\n    force: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--force\", \"-f\", help=\"Reinitialize even if already initialized\"),\n    offline: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--offline\", \"-o\", help=\"Use local templates without network\"),\n    with_config: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--with-config\", \"-c\", help=\"Create se3.config.yaml\"),\n    se3_version: str = typer.Option(SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION, \"--se3-version\", \"-v\", help=\"Specify SE3 version to use\"),\n):\n    \"\"\"Initialize a new SE 3.0 project.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        initialize_project(force, offline, with_config, se3_version)\n    except Exception as e:\n        typer.echo(\n            typer.style(\n                f\"Error during initialization: {str(e)}\",\n                fg=typer.colors.RED,\n            )\n        )\n        raise typer.Exit(1)\n\n# Register sub-typer commands (complex multi-command tools)\napp.add_typer(lint.app, name=\"lint\", help=\"Lint OpenSpec files\")\napp.add_typer(status.app, name=\"status\", help=\"Check project status\")\napp.add_typer(sync.app, name=\"sync\", help=\"Sync output files\")\napp.add_typer(verify.app, name=\"verify\", help=\"Verify spec coverage\")\napp.add_typer(update.app, name=\"update\", help=\"Update SE 3.0 framework to latest version\")\napp.add_typer(collab.app, name=\"collab\", help=\"Manage git-worktree multi-agent collaboration\")\napp.add_typer(commit.app, name=\"commit\", help=\"Commit changes with SE3 verification\")\napp.add_typer(openspec.app, name=\"openspec\", help=\"Manage OpenSpec directory and specs\")\napp.add_typer(human_calls_cmd.app, name=\"human-calls\", help=\"Manage human calls\")\napp.add_typer(human_input.app, name=\"human\", help=\"Manage human input\")\n\n# Register direct commands (simple single-command tools with positional args)\n# These are registered as direct commands to avoid sub-typer nesting issues\n@app.command(name=\"start\")\ndef start_cmd(\n    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n):\n    \"\"\"Start an SE3 session — compute state and return actions for the agent.\"\"\"\n    from .commands.start import run_session_start, print_text_report, print_json_report\n    import json\n    state = run_session_start(project_root)\n    if format == \"json\":\n        print_json_report(state)\n    else:\n        print_text_report(state)\n    raise typer.Exit(code=0 if not state.get(\"actions\") else 1)\n\n@app.command(name=\"work\")\ndef work_cmd(\n    change_name: Optional[str] = typer.Argument(None, help=\"Name of the change to work on\"),\n    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n    new: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--new\", help=\"Create new change with workflow type (bugfix/feature/review/directive)\"),\n    advance: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--advance\", \"-a\", help=\"Mark current step complete and advance to next\"),\n    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n):\n    \"\"\"Start or continue working on a change — the SDD workflow driver.\"\"\"\n    from .commands.work import run_work, print_text_report, print_json_report\n    result = run_work(project_root, change_name, new, advance)\n    if format == \"json\":\n        print_json_report(result)\n    else:\n        print_text_report(result)\n    raise typer.Exit(code=0 if result.get(\"change\") else 1)\n\n@app.command(name=\"done\")\ndef done_cmd(\n    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n):\n    \"\"\"End an SE3 session — compute shutdown actions for the agent.\"\"\"\n    from .commands.done import run_session_done, print_text_report, print_json_report\n    state = run_session_done(project_root)\n    if format == \"json\":\n        print_json_report(state)\n    else:\n        print_text_report(state)\n    raise typer.Exit(code=0)\n\ndef _full_cycle_cmd_impl(\n    description: str,\n    project_root: str,\n    quick: bool,\n    format: str,\n):\n    \"\"\"Implementation of full-cycle command.\"\"\"\n    from .commands.fullcycle import run_full_cycle, print_text_report as fullcycle_print_text, print_json_report as fullcycle_print_json\n    result = run_full_cycle(description, project_root, quick)\n    if format == \"json\":\n        fullcycle_print_json(result)\n    else:\n        fullcycle_print_text(result)\n    raise typer.Exit(code=0 if result.get(\"success\") else 1)\n\n\n@app.command(name=\"full-cycle\")\ndef full_cycle_cmd(\n    description: str = typer.Argument(..., help=\"Description of the work to do\"),\n    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n    quick: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--quick\", \"-q\", help=\"Quick mode - skip formal change creation, use 'small' workflow\"),\n    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n):\n    \"\"\"Run the complete start-work-done workflow in one command.\n\n    This command streamlines simple/quick tasks by combining:\n    1. se3 start - Initialize the session\n    2. se3 work --new - Create a change for the work\n    3. Implementation (performed by agent)\n    4. se3 done - Complete the session\n\n    Examples:\n        se3 full-cycle \"fix login bug\"\n        se3 full-cycle \"add user profile page\" --quick\n        se3 full-cycle \"update documentation\" -q --json\n    \"\"\"\n    _full_cycle_cmd_impl(description, project_root, quick, format)\n\n\n@app.command(name=\"fc\")\ndef fc_cmd(\n    description: str = typer.Argument(..., help=\"Description of the work to do\"),\n    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n    quick: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--quick\", \"-q\", help=\"Quick mode - skip formal change creation, use 'small' workflow\"),\n    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n):\n    \"\"\"Alias for 'full-cycle' - Run the complete start-work-done workflow in one command.\"\"\"\n    _full_cycle_cmd_impl(description, project_root, quick, format)\n\n# Register handoff as a direct command (not a sub-typer)\n@app.command(name=\"handoff\")\ndef handoff_cmd(\n    message: Optional[str] = typer.Argument(None, help=\"Handoff message describing what was done\"),\n    project_root: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Project root directory\"),\n    dry_run: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--dry-run\", help=\"Preview what would happen without executing\"),\n    skip_commit: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--skip-commit\", help=\"Skip automatic commit (use with caution)\"),\n):\n    \"\"\"Handoff control to human — enforcing SE3 commit-before-handoff rule.\"\"\"\n    from .commands.handoff import handoff\n    handoff(message=message, project_root=project_root, dry_run=dry_run, skip_commit=skip_commit)\n\n\n@app.command(name=\"claude-cmd\")\ndef claude_cmd(\n    all_cmds: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--all\", help=\"Output all commands as JSON sorted by priority\"),\n    next_after: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--next\", help=\"Output the next command after the given one\"),\n    project_root: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Project root directory\"),\n):\n    \"\"\"Show configured Claude commands by priority.\n\n    Used by bash scripts to resolve which Claude command to use.\n    \"\"\"\n    from .config import load_claude_commands\n\n    root = Path(project_root) if project_root else Path.cwd()\n    commands = load_claude_commands(root)\n\n    if all_cmds:\n        typer.echo(json.dumps(commands))\n    elif next_after:\n        found = False\n        for i, entry in enumerate(commands):\n            if entry[\"cmd\"] == next_after:\n                if i + 1 < len(commands):\n                    typer.echo(commands[i + 1][\"cmd\"])\n                else:\n                    typer.echo(\"\")  # No next command\n                found = True\n                break\n        if not found:\n            typer.echo(\"\")  # Command not in list\n    else:\n        # Default: output highest-priority command\n        typer.echo(commands[0][\"cmd\"])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app()\n","numLines":244,"startLine":1,"totalLines":244}}}
